WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:21.180
Suddenly Peter was not as carefree as he had been. He was now on the alert.

2
00:00:21.181 --> 00:00:27.459
He looked down in the growing darkness and pointed to the smoke rising from a campfire below.

3
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.926
"See that smoke?

4
00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:33.334
It comes from the camp of the Indians just across the Mysterious River."

5
00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:37.957
Peter explained to the children. "Those are smoke signals.

6
00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:39.601
They are on the war path.

7
00:00:39.602 --> 00:00:44.697
And look," he said, pointing to another part of the island.

8
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:51.062
"There are the pirates getting ready to shoot their cannon, called Long Tom, at Execution Dock.

9
00:00:51.063 --> 00:00:53.319
We need to be on our guard."

10
00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.625
With this, Peter sent Tinker Bell up front to lead the way.

11
00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:03.407
Her glow provided enough light for everyone to see each other and the land below.

12
00:01:03.408 --> 00:01:07.176
All had been quiet in Neverland while Peter was gone.

13
00:01:07.177 --> 00:01:12.432
When Peter was not there, life on the island was always more peaceful.

14
00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:17.364
The fairies and mermaids even took an extra hour to get up in the morning.

15
00:01:17.365 --> 00:01:23.425
Rather than fighting, the pirates and the Lost Boys just made faces at each other when they met.

16
00:01:23.426 --> 00:01:28.372
The Indians planted their corn, and the wild animals looked after their young.

17
00:01:28.373 --> 00:01:32.485
But when Peter arrived, the action began!

18
00:01:32.486 --> 00:01:37.091
Peter told the children about the pirates and their ship, the Jolly Roger.

19
00:01:37.092 --> 00:01:41.951
Their eyes lit up when he talked about the pirates' wicked leader—Captain Hook!

20
00:01:41.952 --> 00:01:49.272
The children had heard of him and his evil reputation. Michael began to cry.

21
00:01:49.273 --> 00:01:54.230
John asked, "Is he as mean and as big as they say?"

22
00:01:54.231 --> 00:02:02.316
"Well, he's a bit smaller now," replied Peter, "because I cut off his right hand."

23
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:07.088
"Then he can't fight?" replied Michael hopefully.

24
00:02:07.089 --> 00:02:11.535
"Oh no, he can fight. He's as fierce as ever.

25
00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:15.643
But now he has an iron hook instead of a right hand.

26
00:02:15.644 --> 00:02:20.092
In fact, he's been known to claw people to death with that hook."

27
00:02:20.093 --> 00:02:25.782
"Well, I wonder what it would be like to meet him!" said John.

28
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:29.881
He was almost looking forward to a pirate adventure.

29
00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:34.817
"Not me, I would be too scared!" cried Michael.

30
00:02:34.818 --> 00:02:41.179
"As captain, there is one thing I demand of each boy who serves under me," said Peter.

31
00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.918
"If we meet Hook in a fight, you must leave him to me."

32
00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:50.213
"Ay, ay, sir," replied both boys.

33
00:02:50.214 --> 00:02:54.875
"But right now, we aren't ready for a fight," Peter declared.

34
00:02:54.876 --> 00:02:57.122
"Let's get out of sight.

35
00:02:57.123 --> 00:03:01.738
The pirates might already have seen us because of Tink's light."

36
00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:06.884
"Tell her to put out her light," the children cried in unison.

37
00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:11.744
"Her light only goes out when she is asleep," said Peter.

38
00:03:11.745 --> 00:03:16.347
"But we can put her in John's top hat."

39
00:03:16.348 --> 00:03:20.760
When Tinker Bell thought Peter would carry the hat, she agreed happily.

40
00:03:20.761 --> 00:03:24.581
But when Peter gave the hat to Wendy, Tink was upset.

41
00:03:24.582 --> 00:03:31.683
After thinking about it, the fairy decided not to make a fuss—at least not just yet.

42
00:03:31.684 --> 00:03:36.013
With Tinker Bell in the hat, the group's guiding light was gone.

43
00:03:36.014 --> 00:03:38.863
They flew on in complete silence.

44
00:03:38.864 --> 00:03:43.777
Suddenly, Peter and the children became enveloped in a ghostly stillness.

45
00:03:43.778 --> 00:03:49.750
"If only something would make a sound . . ." sighed Michael.

46
00:03:49.751 --> 00:03:54.250
As if to answer Michael's wish, there was a huge boom!

47
00:03:54.251 --> 00:03:57.814
The pirates had fired Long Tom into the sky.

48
00:03:57.815 --> 00:04:03.052
The cannon's roar echoed through the mountains and sent the group flying in different directions.

49
00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:07.291
No one was hit, but Peter was thrown far out to sea.

50
00:04:07.292 --> 00:04:13.948
Wendy was blown upward. She still held John's hat with Tinker Bell in it.

51
00:04:13.949 --> 00:04:18.452
Tinker Bell wasn't a bad fairy. Sometimes she was really good.

52
00:04:18.453 --> 00:04:21.812
But at this moment, she was bad.

53
00:04:21.813 --> 00:04:26.916
She hated Wendy because she was jealous of Wendy's feelings for Peter.

54
00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:33.005
It would have been better for Wendy if she had dropped the hat, but Wendy would never have let go.

55
00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:39.529
After the cannon blast, Tinker Bell popped out of the hat and tinkled something in fairy language.

56
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.764
Wendy did not understand.

57
00:04:41.765 --> 00:04:45.449
She assumed the fairy was saying "Follow me."

58
00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:53.476
What else could Wendy do? She followed.
